{"id": "section-body-20727", "title": "Toxic Multinodular Goiter or Thyroid Antibody Positive", "chapterId": "chapter-nineteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "METABOLIC AND ENDOCRINE DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Thyroid Disorders", "Toxic Multinodular Goiter or Thyroid Antibody Positive"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-20727", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Toxic Multinodular Goiter or Thyroid Antibody Positive", "runs": [{"text": "Toxic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Multinodular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Goiter"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Thyroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Antibody"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Positive"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "924"}}, {"id": "body-20728", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Patients with overtly Toxic multinodular goiter or Thyroid antibody are treated with either:", "runs": [{"text": "Patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "overtly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Toxic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "multinodular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "goiter"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Thyroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antibody"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "either:"}]}, {"id": "body-20730", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management S: Radio iodine (131-I) therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Management S: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Radio iodine (131-I) therapy"}]}, {"id": "body-20731", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-20732", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: Thyroidectomy", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Thyroidectomy"}]}, {"id": "body-20733-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Note: Long term, low-dose carbimazole should not be used for either condition except in some elderly", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Long"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "term,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "low-dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "carbimazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "either"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "condition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "except"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "some"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "elderly"}]}, {"id": "body-20735", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Surgery", "runs": [{"text": "Surgery"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-20736", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Patients with overt hyperthyroidism should be rendered euthyroid prior to the procedure with carbimazole pre-treatment (15–40mg daily, divided into 2–3doses a day for 4–8 weeks then a maintenance dose of 5–15mg, taken 24 hourly) with or without beta–adrenergic blockade (e.g. propranolol 1—40mg 6hourly). Preoperative iodine should not be used in this setting.", "runs": [{"text": "Patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "overt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hyperthyroidism"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rendered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "euthyroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "prior"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "procedure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "carbimazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pre-treatment (15–40mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "divided"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "into"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2–3doses"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "4–8"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "then"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maintenance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5–15mg,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "taken"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hourly)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "beta–adrenergic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blockade"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "propranolol"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1—40mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "6hourly)."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Preoperative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "iodine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "this "}, {"text": "setting."}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "924"}}, {"id": "body-20737", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Following thyroidectomy for Toxic multinodular goiter, it is suggested that serum calcium or intact parathyroid hormone levels be measured, and that calcitriol and oral calcium supplementation (maximum 1,200mg of calcium per day in two divided doses) be administered based on these results.", "runs": [{"text": "Following"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "thyroidectomy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Toxic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "multinodular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "goiter,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suggested"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "serum calcium or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "intact"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parathyroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hormone levels"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "measured,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "calcitriol"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "calcium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "supplementation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(maximum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1,200mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "calcium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "per"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "two divided doses) be administered based on these results."}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "924"}}, {"id": "body-20738", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Following surgery for Toxic multinodular goiter, thyroid hormone replacement should be started at a dose appropriate for the patient’s weight (0.8µg/lb. or 1.7µg/kg) and age, with elderly patients needing somewhat less. TSH should be measured every 1–2months until stable, and then annually.", "runs": [{"text": "Following surgery for Toxic multinodular goiter, thyroid hormone replacement should be started at a dose appropriate for the patient’s weight (0.8µg/lb. or 1.7µg/kg) and age, with elderly patients needing somewhat less. TSH should be measured every 1–2months until stable, and then annually."}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "924"}}, {"id": "body-20739", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Radioiodine", "runs": [{"text": "Radioiodine"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-20740", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Radioactive iodine therapy should be used for retreatment of persistent or recurrent hyperthyroidism following inadequate surgery for Toxic multinodular goiter or Thyroid antibody.", "runs": [{"text": "Radioactive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "iodine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"te